shared API / scientific intake / recorded output,datasets.js,"applicable declared task / loaded, empty, busy, failed or recorded result branch","<h2>Data & analysis</h2><p>Choose a question, add data, review, then analyze. Saved files can be reused in either role.</p><div class=""actions""><button id=""registry-public"">Add reviewed public ER datasets</button><button id=""registry-space"">Discover datasets in SPACE ↗</button></div><div class=""registry-filters""><label for=""registry-search"">Find a dataset<input id=""registry-search"" type=""search"" placeholder=""Name, accession or version ID""></label><label for=""registry-status"">Preparation<select id=""registry-status""><option value="""">All versions</option><option value=""prepared"">Prepared</option><option value=""acquired"">Acquired originals</option></select></label><label class=""check""><input id=""registry-fixtures"" type=""checkbox"">Include software checks</label><label class=""check""><input id=""registry-archived"" type=""checkbox"">Show archived studies</label><p id=""registry-count"" role=""status""></p></div><div id=""registry-list""></div><p id=""registry-no-match"" hidden>No dataset versions match. Clear the search or change the preparation filter.</p><div id=""registry-detail""></div><details><summary>Import a prepared expression dataset</summary><form id=""registry-import""><label for=""registry-import-name"">Dataset display name</label><input id=""registry-import-name"" required maxlength=""200""><label for=""registry-expression"">Processed expression (CSV/TSV)</label><input id=""registry-expression"" type=""file"" accept="".csv,.tsv"" required><label for=""registry-metadata"">Sample metadata (CSV/TSV)</label><input id=""registry-metadata"" type=""file"" accept="".csv,.tsv"" required><label for=""registry-manifest"">BRACE dataset manifest (JSON)</label><input id=""registry-manifest"" type=""file"" accept="".json"" required><button>Validate and register dataset</button></form></details><form id=""registry-analysis""><h3>Run an analysis</h3><div id=""registry-empty"" role=""status"" hidden></div><label for=""registry-study"">Study</label><select id=""registry-study""><option value="""">New study</option></select><label for=""registry-name"">Study name</label><input id=""registry-name"" required maxlength=""200"" placeholder=""Name this research question""><label for=""registry-task"">Scientific task</label><select id=""registry-task"">${Object.entries(
    label,
  )
    .map(([key, text]) => `<option value=""${key}"">${text}</option>`)
    .join(
      """",
    )}</select><div class=""cohort-grid""><div><label for=""registry-source"">Source / prediction dataset</label><select id=""registry-source""></select></div><div id=""registry-target-field""><label for=""registry-target"">Target dataset</label><select id=""registry-target""></select></div></div><details id=""registry-race""><summary>Review biological contrast and exploratory processing policy</summary><p>Use exact prepared metadata labels for the same biological contrast in both studies. Create a reviewed phenotype version first if the vocabularies differ.</p><div class=""cohort-grid""><div><label for=""registry-positive"">Positive-group label</label><input id=""registry-positive""><label for=""registry-positive-definition"">Positive-group biological definition</label><input id=""registry-positive-definition""></div><div><label for=""registry-negative"">Negative-group label</label><input id=""registry-negative""><label for=""registry-negative-definition"">Negative-group biological definition</label><input id=""registry-negative-definition""></div></div><label class=""check""><input id=""registry-processing-review"" type=""checkbox"">I accept exploratory within-study effect comparisons despite declared processing differences.</label><label for=""registry-selection-count"">Source selection cap</label><input id=""registry-selection-count"" type=""number"" min=""1"" max=""1000"" step=""1"" value=""20""><p class=""help"">Freeze up to this many source features with BH q ≤ 0.05, ranked by absolute Hedges’ g. 20 preserves the historical example. Choose before inspecting the target; the 1–1000 range is a software limit, not a biological optimum.</p><label class=""check""><input id=""registry-review"" type=""checkbox"">I reviewed the source and target biological group definitions and processing limitations.</label></details><div class=""actions""><button id=""registry-check"" type=""submit"">Check selected datasets</button><button id=""registry-run"" type=""button"" class=""primary"" disabled>Compute checked analysis</button></div></form><div id=""registry-checks"" aria-live=""polite""></div><details><summary>Apply a previously frozen BRACE baseline</summary><p>Reuses an existing source-trained JSON freeze. No fitting on the new target. Unlabeled targets produce predictions with no accuracy metrics.</p><form id=""registry-replay""><label for=""registry-replay-name"">Replay study name</label><input id=""registry-replay-name"" required maxlength=""200""><label for=""registry-freeze"">Original source-trained run</label><select id=""registry-freeze"" required></select><label for=""registry-replay-target"">Target dataset version</label><select id=""registry-replay-target"" required></select><button>Apply frozen baseline</button></form></details>","Read exact parser errors, warnings, recorded identifiers or methods",generated_template,The surrounding source branch and data checks must hold; dynamic values are actual saved or user-supplied fields,"Literal label/message or exact generated view: Data & analysis Choose a question, add data, review, then analyze. Saved files can be reused in either role. Add reviewed public ER datasets Discover datasets in SPACE ↗ Find a dataset Preparation All versions Prepared Acquired originals Include software checks Show archived studies No dataset versions match. Clear the search or change the preparation filter. Import a prepared expression dataset Dataset display name Processed expression (CSV/TSV) Sample metadata (CSV/TSV) BRACE dataset manifest (JSON) Validate and register dataset Run an analysis Study New study Study name Scientific task ${Object.entries( label, ) .map(([key, text]) => ` ${text} `) .join( """", )} Source / prediction dataset Target dataset Review biological contrast and exploratory processing policy Use exact prepared metadata labels for the same biological contrast in both studies. Create a reviewed phenotype version first if the vocabularies differ. Positive-group label Positive-group biological definition Negative-group label Negative-group biological definition I accept exploratory within-study effect comparisons despite declared processing differences. Source selection cap Freeze up to this many source features with BH q ≤ 0.05, ranked by absolute Hedges’ g. 20 preserves the historical example. Choose before inspecting the target; the 1–1000 range is a software limit, not a biological optimum. I reviewed the source and target biological group definitions and processing limitations. Check selected datasets Compute checked analysis Apply a previously frozen BRACE baseline Reuses an existing source-trained JSON freeze. No fitting on the new target. Unlabeled targets produce predictions with no accuracy metrics. Replay study name Original source-trained run Target dataset version Apply frozen baseline",Existing scientific contract and issue code; raw data fields retain exact saved meaning,"Specific handler, generated artifact or recorded field at the source location; no invented completion",brace_app/static/js/datasets.js:374; sha256=7fbdb359ce029dcadb05b0f35ac80e90bf6c6a2b8f9d5622c63af1239f3ffb92,Dynamic declarations are unverified; scientific thresholds and denominators require adjacent definitions or recorded methods,keep,D3_API_REGRESSION
