shared API / scientific intake / recorded output,guide.js,"applicable declared task / loaded, empty, busy, failed or recorded result branch","<h3>Expression and metadata tables for two studies</h3><p>Use processed, normalized human bulk gene-expression measurements. The same gene identifiers and biological contrast must be meaningful in both studies.</p><div class=""file-guide-pair""><div><strong>1. Expression matrix · CSV/TSV</strong><p class=""help"">Genes in rows. Samples in columns. First column: <code>feature_id</code>.</p><table><tr><th>feature_id</th><th>S01</th><th>S02</th></tr><tr><td>2099</td><td>8.2</td><td>6.4</td></tr><tr><td>135112</td><td>7.1</td><td>9.3</td></tr></table></div><div><strong>2. Sample metadata · CSV/TSV</strong><p class=""help"">One row per sample. The sample IDs must match the matrix.</p><table><tr><th>sample_id</th><th>condition</th><th>patient_id</th></tr><tr><td>S01</td><td>case</td><td>P01</td></tr><tr><td>S02</td><td>control</td><td>P02</td></tr></table></div></div><p class=""help"">These cells illustrate the file shape; they are not a research dataset.</p><div class=""guide-note""><strong>No JSON editing required.</strong><br>In setup, describe the organism, identifier type, normalized values and processing. BRACE creates the dataset declaration. Existing BRACE declarations can also be selected.</div><h3>Which study goes where?</h3><p><strong>Source:</strong> choose genes or train the supported baseline here. <strong>Target:</strong> test the frozen choice here. Use independent studies and equivalent group definitions; sample IDs do not need to match across studies.</p><p class=""help"">RACE accepts unpaired, normalized log2 microarrays. The baseline requires normal/tumor labels. Distribution comparison also supports declared normalized RNA-seq types. 25 MiB/file · 25,000 features · 500 samples per study.</p><div class=""actions""><button id=""guide-expression"" class=""primary"">Set up expression studies</button><button id=""guide-public"">Open the real ER example</button><a href=""/api/templates"" download>Download format examples</a></div>","Read exact parser errors, warnings, recorded identifiers or methods",generated_template,The surrounding source branch and data checks must hold; dynamic values are actual saved or user-supplied fields,"Literal label/message or exact generated view: Expression and metadata tables for two studies Use processed, normalized human bulk gene-expression measurements. The same gene identifiers and biological contrast must be meaningful in both studies. 1. Expression matrix · CSV/TSV Genes in rows. Samples in columns. First column: feature_id . feature_id S01 S02 2099 8.2 6.4 135112 7.1 9.3 2. Sample metadata · CSV/TSV One row per sample. The sample IDs must match the matrix. sample_id condition patient_id S01 case P01 S02 control P02 These cells illustrate the file shape; they are not a research dataset. No JSON editing required. In setup, describe the organism, identifier type, normalized values and processing. BRACE creates the dataset declaration. Existing BRACE declarations can also be selected. Which study goes where? Source: choose genes or train the supported baseline here. Target: test the frozen choice here. Use independent studies and equivalent group definitions; sample IDs do not need to match across studies. RACE accepts unpaired, normalized log2 microarrays. The baseline requires normal/tumor labels. Distribution comparison also supports declared normalized RNA-seq types. 25 MiB/file · 25,000 features · 500 samples per study. Set up expression studies Open the real ER example Download format examples",Existing scientific contract and issue code; raw data fields retain exact saved meaning,"Specific handler, generated artifact or recorded field at the source location; no invented completion",brace_app/static/js/guide.js:5; sha256=3cc51de3f63fe121ef2ca758c35e931bca0b2ec500ca7e11ac0a3fd4677f051b,Dynamic declarations are unverified; scientific thresholds and denominators require adjacent definitions or recorded methods,keep,D3_API_REGRESSION
shared API / scientific intake / recorded output,guide.js,"applicable declared task / loaded, empty, busy, failed or recorded result branch","<h3>Saved prediction table</h3><p>Use a CSV/TSV with one record per row. The true label is the known reference; the predicted label is what the model returned.</p><div class=""table-scroll"" tabindex=""0"" role=""group"" aria-label=""Scrollable data table""><table><tr><th>sample_id</th><th>true_label</th><th>predicted_label</th><th>score_case</th><th>score_control</th></tr><tr><td>record_1</td><td>case</td><td>case</td><td>0.96</td><td>0.04</td></tr><tr><td>record_2</td><td>control</td><td>case</td><td>0.70</td><td>0.30</td></tr></table></div><p class=""help"">Illustrative rows, not measured performance. <code>sample_id</code> is a unique record key and can refer to any classification domain.</p><div class=""guide-note""><strong>Class scores are optional.</strong><br>For confidence filtering, provide a separate probability column for every declared class. Each row must contain finite values from 0 to 1 that sum to 1. Scores are not assumed calibrated.</div><p>In setup, enter the model classes, label origin and optional score-column mapping. You can evaluate class-only predictions without any probability columns.</p><p class=""help"">Classification only · 25 MiB/file · 50,000 records. No organism or expression matrix is required.</p><div class=""actions""><button id=""guide-predictions"" class=""primary"">Set up a prediction table</button><button id=""guide-historical"">Explore saved CancerShift predictions</button></div>","Read exact parser errors, warnings, recorded identifiers or methods",generated_template,The surrounding source branch and data checks must hold; dynamic values are actual saved or user-supplied fields,"Literal label/message or exact generated view: Saved prediction table Use a CSV/TSV with one record per row. The true label is the known reference; the predicted label is what the model returned. sample_id true_label predicted_label score_case score_control record_1 case case 0.96 0.04 record_2 control case 0.70 0.30 Illustrative rows, not measured performance. sample_id is a unique record key and can refer to any classification domain. Class scores are optional. For confidence filtering, provide a separate probability column for every declared class. Each row must contain finite values from 0 to 1 that sum to 1. Scores are not assumed calibrated. In setup, enter the model classes, label origin and optional score-column mapping. You can evaluate class-only predictions without any probability columns. Classification only · 25 MiB/file · 50,000 records. No organism or expression matrix is required. Set up a prediction table Explore saved CancerShift predictions",Existing scientific contract and issue code; raw data fields retain exact saved meaning,"Specific handler, generated artifact or recorded field at the source location; no invented completion",brace_app/static/js/guide.js:6; sha256=3cc51de3f63fe121ef2ca758c35e931bca0b2ec500ca7e11ac0a3fd4677f051b,Dynamic declarations are unverified; scientific thresholds and denominators require adjacent definitions or recorded methods,keep,D3_API_REGRESSION
shared API / scientific intake / recorded output,guide.js,"applicable declared task / loaded, empty, busy, failed or recorded result branch","<h3>Have a report ZIP, raw reads or a model file?</h3><ul><li><strong>EMBRACE evidence ZIP:</strong> an output package. Extract it and open <code>research_summary.html</code>. To recompute, use the matching original expression/metadata files or prediction table; raw uploads are not in the evidence ZIP.</li><li><strong>FASTQ, CEL or raw count files:</strong> prepare normalized bulk measurements with an appropriate scientific workflow first. BRACE does not align reads or normalize raw assays.</li><li><strong>Trained model / checkpoint:</strong> run it in its original environment and export predictions with known labels. BRACE does not execute uploaded models.</li><li><strong>Excel workbook:</strong> export the relevant sheet as UTF-8 CSV/TSV, then check the required column names.</li><li><strong>Unlabeled target measurements:</strong> choose distribution comparison. It reports measured differences, not target accuracy.</li></ul><div class=""guide-note"">The included ER example already contains curated, normalized source and target files, verified sample labels and a saved exploratory result.</div><div class=""actions""><button id=""guide-public"" class=""primary"">Open the ready-to-use example</button><button id=""guide-shift"">Compare dataset distributions</button></div>","Read exact parser errors, warnings, recorded identifiers or methods",generated_template,The surrounding source branch and data checks must hold; dynamic values are actual saved or user-supplied fields,"Literal label/message or exact generated view: Have a report ZIP, raw reads or a model file? EMBRACE evidence ZIP: an output package. Extract it and open research_summary.html . To recompute, use the matching original expression/metadata files or prediction table; raw uploads are not in the evidence ZIP. FASTQ, CEL or raw count files: prepare normalized bulk measurements with an appropriate scientific workflow first. BRACE does not align reads or normalize raw assays. Trained model / checkpoint: run it in its original environment and export predictions with known labels. BRACE does not execute uploaded models. Excel workbook: export the relevant sheet as UTF-8 CSV/TSV, then check the required column names. Unlabeled target measurements: choose distribution comparison. It reports measured differences, not target accuracy. The included ER example already contains curated, normalized source and target files, verified sample labels and a saved exploratory result. Open the ready-to-use example Compare dataset distributions",Existing scientific contract and issue code; raw data fields retain exact saved meaning,"Specific handler, generated artifact or recorded field at the source location; no invented completion",brace_app/static/js/guide.js:7; sha256=3cc51de3f63fe121ef2ca758c35e931bca0b2ec500ca7e11ac0a3fd4677f051b,Dynamic declarations are unverified; scientific thresholds and denominators require adjacent definitions or recorded methods,keep,D3_API_REGRESSION
