RACE / FACE,race.js,"applicable declared task / loaded, empty, busy, failed or recorded result branch","<details class=""selection-method""><summary>${a.source_features_screened.toLocaleString()} prepared features → ${a.source_q_passing.toLocaleString()} source FDR passes → ${a.selected} frozen (cap ${rule.max_genes})</summary><p>The prepared matrix is the tested universe, not a complete transcriptome census. Source-only Welch tests compare ${esc(meta.positive)} minus ${esc(meta.negative)}. Benjamini–Hochberg (BH) adjusts the entire source family at q ≤ 0.05. Qualifying features are ranked by absolute Hedges’ g, then identifier; the declared cap freezes the analysis set before target testing. It is not a display limit or biological optimum.</p><p>Hedges’ g is a standardized within-cohort mean difference, not prediction accuracy. Welch’s two-sided test evaluates equal group means under independent observations, allowing unequal variances. Target BH correction covers all ${a.selected} frozen hypotheses; unavailable tests enter as p=1 in that family. A q value is an adjusted p value, not the probability a finding is true. FDR concerns the expected false-discovery proportion under its assumptions.</p><p>95% intervals describe each mean difference. They are pointwise, not simultaneous or adjusted for source selection. Matching direction and target q ≤ 0.05 define support under this exploratory protocol. No classifier was trained. Rerunning selection caps after viewing the target is sensitivity analysis, not independent confirmation.</p></details>",Inspect source-selected associations and within-study measurements,generated_template,The surrounding source branch and data checks must hold; dynamic values are actual saved or user-supplied fields,"Literal label/message or exact generated view: ${a.source_features_screened.toLocaleString()} prepared features → ${a.source_q_passing.toLocaleString()} source FDR passes → ${a.selected} frozen (cap ${rule.max_genes}) The prepared matrix is the tested universe, not a complete transcriptome census. Source-only Welch tests compare ${esc(meta.positive)} minus ${esc(meta.negative)}. Benjamini–Hochberg (BH) adjusts the entire source family at q ≤ 0.05. Qualifying features are ranked by absolute Hedges’ g, then identifier; the declared cap freezes the analysis set before target testing. It is not a display limit or biological optimum. Hedges’ g is a standardized within-cohort mean difference, not prediction accuracy. Welch’s two-sided test evaluates equal group means under independent observations, allowing unequal variances. Target BH correction covers all ${a.selected} frozen hypotheses; unavailable tests enter as p=1 in that family. A q value is an adjusted p value, not the probability a finding is true. FDR concerns the expected false-discovery proportion under its assumptions. 95% intervals describe each mean difference. They are pointwise, not simultaneous or adjusted for source selection. Matching direction and target q ≤ 0.05 define support under this exploratory protocol. No classifier was trained. Rerunning selection caps after viewing the target is sensitivity analysis, not independent confirmation.","Full frozen family, signed within-study effects, target BH q <=0.05; separate cohort axes","Specific handler, generated artifact or recorded field at the source location; no invented completion",brace_app/static/js/race.js:19; sha256=c893e9449df88a2d0851cabdf105ad33fdf0eb4b12891f0d983e1a94daf2252d,Dynamic declarations are unverified; scientific thresholds and denominators require adjacent definitions or recorded methods,keep,D3_PUBLIC_RACE_FACE
